body='''<div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">History comparison v0.1 · development</div><h1>Same coarse code. Different retained histories.</h1><p class="lede">A center-star and a barycentric refinement preserve the old tetrahedron. Matching frequencies permits an unrestricted encoding, but preserving vertex symmetry forbids that complete encoding under the declared metrics.</p></div><aside class="callout"><strong>Conditional comparison · native source law open</strong><p>All results use affine retractions, unit-detail calibration and a fixed internal rate. No physical promotion; independent human review pending. These claims do not select the native metric or refinement event.</p></aside>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Compare every retained direction</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Carrier</th><th>Total directions</th><th>Details</th><th>√5 detail pairs</th><th>S4-trivial √5 pairs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Original tetrahedron</td><td>15</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Center-star 1→4</td><td>29</td><td>14</td><td>7</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Barycentric</td><td>149</td><td>134</td><td>10</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The common coarse code retains seven frequency2 pairs and one harmonic direction. The star adds seven √5 pairs. Barycentric has enough matching frequencies, but none of its √5 modes is invariant under all24 original vertex permutations.</p><p>These spectra belong to H=RᵀR+QᵀQ, Q=I−SR and the corresponding weighted generator. They are not raw unit-metric fine spectra.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Which notion of equivalence?</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Comparison</th><th>Result</th><th>What it retains</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Coarse transfer SsRb</td><td>Exact, but lossy</td><td>Old15 directions; kills134 barycentric details</td></tr><tr><td>Full terminal bijection</td><td>NO-GO</td><td>Dimensions29 and149 differ</td></tr><tr><td>Star→bary generator embedding</td><td>Exists without symmetry</td><td>All29 source directions; nonunique spectral encoding</td></tr><tr><td>S4-equivariant generator embedding</td><td>NO-GO under this contract</td><td>Required invariant √5 pair is absent from target</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>A comparison must preserve both the stated dynamics and the required symmetry representation. Frequency counts alone do not establish history covariance. Changing metrics, rates, symmetry demands or adding carriers requires a new test.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Keep the outgoing record</h2><p>A reversible transfer can retain all data by adding14 target-detail directions and keeping134 old-detail directions as an outgoing record.</p><div class="callout"><p class="form">149 input +14 prepared →29 target +134 record =163 directions</p><p>(Sb c+zb, ws) →(Ss c+ws, zb)</p></div><p>Both sides have squared norm ||c||²+||zb||²+||ws||². With blank ws=0, the old detail record still exists. This is an information-preserving direct-sum transfer, not an acquired clock, physical gate, complete generator equivalence or free reset.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>New coordinates do not create a detail source</h2><p>If A is H-skew and AS=SA0, the coarse image and its orthogonal detail complement are invariant. A blank detail sector stays blank. Exact inheritance therefore cannot also supply autonomous coarse-to-detail excitation.</p><p>A closed skew coupling C can seed detail only with reciprocal coarse feedback and a nonzero inheritance defect. External forcing f instead gives ż=Adz+Qf and a norm-work rate2〈x,f〉H. Either route needs a selected source law and acquisition ledger.</p><p>Source C0656 funds its1→4 event with a same-address C4 launch stock3q². That historical ledger is not the new metric detail norm or a conversion into Qf. A moving metric, prepared seed or recorded jump remains another explicitly typed option.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">05</div><div><h2>Next: declare the excitation interface</h2><p>Specify the seed, forcing, coupling or jump; state clock/event conditions, retained records, donor and reset costs; fix the observer. Then test symmetry and generator compatibility before any native or physical claim.</p><p>This comparison advances the development lane only. Same-sequence hierarchy coherence remains intact; native metric, observer and detail-source adoption remain open.</p></div></section><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/releases/UD_REFINEMENT_HISTORY_AND_DETAIL_SOURCE_v0.1.zip" download>Download exact proofs and replay ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/history-comparison-v0.1/UD_REFINEMENT_HISTORY_AND_DETAIL_SOURCE_v0.1.md">Full theorem record</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/history-comparison-v0.1/HISTORY_COMPARISON_EXACT_RECEIPT_v0.1.json">Exact replay receipt</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/history-comparison-v0.1/detail-history-source-review.md">AI source audit</a><a class="text-link" href="/dependencies/?node=HC-NEXT">Dependency gate</a><a class="text-link" href="/refinement-tower/">Same-sequence hierarchy</a></div>'''
